    "description": "I design, develop, and code software for three primary company initiatives: EDA Cloud (2014-present), Pre-RTL Standard Cell and Memory Modeling (2009-2013), and Open Access Data Structure Design & Support (2007-2009). I present research findings to outside collaborators. Among my accomplishments:\n    \n❖EDA Cloud Initiative: \n→ Spearheaded the Cadence Cloud Initiative and successful implementation of IaaS Cloud for Verification IP business unit.   \n→ Designed and developed a push-button framework that enabled user to automatically submit jobs on either the Cloud or on-premises farm, based on design type.  \n\n❖Pre-RTL Standard Cell & Memory Modeling:\n→ Led the standard cell and memory modeling for the pre-RTL chip estimation tool.\n→ Independently managed all modeling products including Stdcell, IO, and Memory. \n→ Designed and developed technology scaling, layer stackup, and technology validation features for Pre-RTL chip planning.\n→ Responsible for supporting proliferation efforts and product evaluation with customers. \n→ Provided breakthrough solution for modeling product packaging.\n \n❖Open Access Data Structure Design & Support:\n→ Designed and implemented automated test architecture that reduced time for build and test tasks.\n→ Developed a performance measurement tool for capturing different performance parameters.\n→ Evaluated performance of FirstEncounter with Open Access as a native database.\n\n❖Infrastructure Development/Support Projects:\n→ Developed a patentable design to migrate source code from ClearCase to Perforce.\n→ Developed Perforce/Netbeans plug-in for Web developers and other groups at Cadence",
